// Main is valid and only ever calls Lib.used; Lib.unused (whose body has an
// undefined identifier) is never imported here nor called, so it is never
// emitted. The reject therefore can only come from the acceptance pass walking
// the imported module's bodies regardless of reachability — the property that
// removing the entry-module-only verify gate gave us (root③(iv)).
use @Std/Io only { print }
use ./Lib only { used }

fn main() {
    print(used())
}
